sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) / Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) anisotropic differential adhesion and polarized T1 junctional intercalation in convergent extension — MorphoEval overall 91.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2003-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation.py` (91.9/100, up from 61.2/100 in Pass 1; +30.7 overall). The remediated script integrates the 64-cell Zajac et al. (2000, 2003) anisotropic differential adhesion law J(theta) = J_0 - Delta_J cos(2*theta) coupled with Bertet et al. (2004) planar-polarized Myosin II vertical junction contraction and irreversible T1 quartet resolution, verifies midpoint RK2 convergence of the pure-shear ODE against R_CE(t) = R_0 exp(2*dot_epsilon_T1*t) (L2 relative error = 1.19e-7), enforces exact 2D tissue area conservation L_AP * L_ML = A_0, reproduces all 5 experimental regimes (Pearson r = 1.0000, RMSE = 0.0042), sweeps a 15x15 2D parameter morphospace, and validates cellular aspect ratio and angular rose polarity against the confocal Xenopus explant specimen (`convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg`, L/W = 4.945 vs 0.962, rose angular r = 0.9677), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_093_convergent_extension_intercalation.lean`. Overall 91.9/100 (faithfulness 92.0, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/convergent_extension_intercalation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2003-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 737138 B, 2408×1428 px, artifact_sha256 b0a09bba189a3e24e1c50bba4f1328917e09f847c0548cefb8da60430e7154e0 (sha256 b0a09bba189a3e24e1c50bba4f1328917e09f847c0548cefb8da60430e7154e0), spec_fingerprint 70c0d2a81cec84a4a194e326ee3833640573b76865ed3d8f4c5ff14fdbf4448d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 70c0d2a81cec84a4a194e326ee3833640573b76865ed3d8f4c5ff14fdbf4448d; artifact_sha256: b0a09bba189a3e24e1c50bba4f1328917e09f847c0548cefb8da60430e7154e0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg=0c2620bce19ad4cf..., datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/convergent_extension_intercalation_reference.json=5e3d70d1a6711a38..., datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/scout_manifest.json=66a1e6f4d0f0a745...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-convergent-extension-intercalation-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) Phys. Rev. Lett. 85:2022 / J. Theor. Biol. 222:247-259 anisotropic differential adhesion energy J(theta) = J_0 - Delta_J cos(2*theta) and pure-shear convergent-extension aspect ratio scaling R_CE(t) = R_0 exp(2*dot_epsilon_T1*t) | Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) Nature 429:667-671 planar-polarized Myosin II enrichment on vertical/AP-facing type-1 junctions driving irreversible 4-way T1 vertex resolution into horizontal/ML type-3 junctions; reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell planar-polarized T1 intercalation lattice solver with exact incompressible 2D tissue area conservation (L_AP * L_ML = A_0, error < 1e-15) and midpoint RK2 ODE convergence verification (L2 relative error 1.19e-7) | 5-regime genetic & mechanical perturbation simulator (Wild-Type R_CE=3.859, T1/cell=1.45; Moderate Anisotropy R_CE=2.375; Xdd1/PCP mutant R_CE=1.566; Myosin II zip/sqh mutant R_CE=1.204; Isotropic Null Control R_CE=1.000, T1/cell=0.00; Pearson r=1.0000, RMSE=0.0042) | Automated confocal Xenopus explant segmentation and rose-diagram angular correlation on convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg (chordamesoderm L/W=4.945 vs animal cap 0.962; nematic S_2=0.613 vs 0.094; rose angular correlation r=0.9677); transfer_boundary: 2D planar 64-cell intercalating tissue sheet and 4-cell T1 quartet junction mechanics mapped to Xenopus chordamesoderm explants and Drosophila germband extension; does_not_claim: Full 3D multicellular rosette (5+ cell vertex) resolution or explicit subcellular F-actin/EB3 microtubule polymerization reaction-diffusion kinetics." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.919"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

